examples.question_text:
The graph shows a company's share price at the beginning of each month.
[tikz]
% mathsmap-diagram-colours {"version":1,"kind":"graph","base":[],"semantic":[{"name":"shareSeries","hex":"268CFF","reason":"One share-price time series and its sampled price markers"}],"reference":"Investments and Loans 1_Investment, Dividends Q8(a)-(c), lines 1647-1663 adaptation"}
\definecolor{shareSeries}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridColour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=20mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[gridColour,very thin,xstep=9mm,ystep=2mm] (0,0) grid (5,2);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(5.6,0) node[below right] {Month};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,2.2) node[above left] {Price (\$)};
\foreach \x/\m in {1/Jan,2/Feb,3/Mar,4/Apr,5/May} \node[below] at (\x,0) {\m};
\foreach \y/\v in {0/6.00,0.5/6.50,1/7.00,1.5/7.50,2/8.00} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {\v};
\draw[very thick,shareSeries] (1,1.7)--(2,1.1)--(3,0.4)--(4,1.6)--(5,1.3);
\foreach \pt in {(1,1.7),(2,1.1),(3,0.4),(4,1.6),(5,1.3)} \fill[shareSeries] \pt circle (2pt);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(a) Read the price in May.
(b) Find the dollar decrease from January to May.
(c) Find the percentage decrease from January to May, correct to two decimal places.

examples.solution_text:
(a) Each small horizontal division is $\$0.10$. May is $13$ small divisions above $\$6.00$.
$\begin{aligned}\text{Price in May}&=6.00+13\times0.10\\&=\$7.30\end{aligned}$
The dashed guides identify the January and May prices.
[tikz]
\definecolor{shareSeries}{HTML}{268CFF}
\definecolor{gridColour}{HTML}{CCCCCC}
\begin{tikzpicture}[x=9mm,y=20mm,every node/.style={text=black,font=\fontsize{10}{12}\selectfont}]
\draw[gridColour,very thin,xstep=9mm,ystep=2mm] (0,0) grid (5,2);
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(5.6,0) node[below right] {Month};
\draw[->,black] (0,0)--(0,2.2) node[above left] {Price (\$)};
\foreach \x/\m in {1/Jan,2/Feb,3/Mar,4/Apr,5/May} \node[below] at (\x,0) {\m};
\foreach \y/\v in {0/6.00,0.5/6.50,1/7.00,1.5/7.50,2/8.00} \node[left,font=\fontsize{8.5}{10}\selectfont] at (0,\y) {\v};
\draw[very thick,shareSeries] (1,1.7)--(2,1.1)--(3,0.4)--(4,1.6)--(5,1.3);
\foreach \pt in {(1,1.7),(2,1.1),(3,0.4),(4,1.6),(5,1.3)} \fill[shareSeries] \pt circle (2pt);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,1.7)--(1,1.7)--(1,0);
\draw[black,dashed] (0,1.3)--(5,1.3)--(5,0);
\path (1,1.7) node[above right] {\$7.70};
\path (5,1.3) node[above right] {\$7.30};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
(b) January is $17$ small divisions above $\$6.00$.
$\begin{aligned}\text{Price in January}&=6.00+17\times0.10\\&=\$7.70\end{aligned}$
$\begin{aligned}\text{Decrease}&=7.70-7.30\\&=\$0.40\end{aligned}$
(c) Divide the decrease by the initial price.
$\begin{aligned}\text{Percentage decrease}&=\dfrac{0.40}{7.70}\times100\%\\&\approx5.19\%\end{aligned}$
